---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import legal from '../config/legal.json';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Be Deutsch Website and Android App"
  description="Privacy information for the Be Deutsch website and the Be Deutsch A1 Foundations Android app."
>
  <div id="top"></div>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main id="main-content" class="legal-page">
    <Section class="page-hero legal-hero" tone="canvas" labelledby="privacy-page-title">
      <div class="legal-hero__grid">
        <div class="page-hero__copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
          <h1 id="privacy-page-title">Privacy information for the website and Android app.</h1>
          <p class="page-hero__lead">
            This page separates the data practices of the public website from those of Be Deutsch
            A1 Foundations for Android.
          </p>
          <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: 26 October 2026</p>
        </div>
        <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Privacy page sections">
          <p>On this page</p>
          <a href="#website-privacy">A. Website privacy</a>
          <a href="#app-privacy">B. Android app privacy</a>
          <a href="#privacy-rights">Your rights</a>
          <a href="#privacy-contact">Contact</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </Section>

    {!legal.legalReady && (
      <div class="release-warning" role="status">
        <div class="container release-warning__inner">
          <strong>Pre-publication legal status</strong>
          <p>
            A legally suitable service address and confirmation of the complete legal provider name
            are still required. The production release check remains blocked until both are resolved.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    )}

    <Section id="website-privacy" tone="white" labelledby="website-privacy-title">
      <div class="legal-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">A. Website privacy</p>
        <h2 id="website-privacy-title">How the Be Deutsch website handles data.</h2>

        <h3>Controller and contact</h3>
        <p>
          The controller for this website is <strong>{legal.providerName}</strong>, a private
          individual / natural person operating from Germany.
        </p>
        <dl class="legal-facts legal-facts--stacked">
          <div>
            <dt>Service address</dt>
            <dd>
              <address>
                {legal.serviceAddress.street}<br />
                {legal.serviceAddress.postalCode} {legal.serviceAddress.city}<br />
                {legal.serviceAddress.country}
              </address>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div><dt>Email</dt><dd><a href={`mailto:${legal.supportEmail}`}>{legal.supportEmail}</a></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><a href={legal.phoneHref}>{legal.phoneDisplay}</a></dd></div>
        </dl>

        <h3>Website code and local vocabulary progress</h3>
        <p>
          The website code does not set cookies, run analytics, use tracking pixels, show advertising,
          load external fonts, embed third-party media, offer a newsletter or provide a contact form.
          The vocabulary course works without registration.
        </p>
        <p>
          The vocabulary course uses your browser’s local storage to remember your selected translation
          language, feedback-sound setting, lesson position, viewed and studied vocabulary IDs, and quiz
          scores and attempt counts. These learning records stay in that browser. The website code does
          not send them to Be Deutsch or an analytics service, and they are not synchronized across devices.
        </p>
        <p>
          Local progress remains until you clear it or your browser removes site data. “Clear local
          progress” in the course resets learning progress and quiz scores while keeping your language
          and sound preferences. Clearing this website’s data in browser settings also removes those
          preferences. If storage is unavailable, learning remains available but progress may not survive
          navigation or a reload. Page, illustration and audio requests still reach the hosting provider
          as described below.
        </p>

        <h3>Hosting through GitHub Pages</h3>
        <p>
          The website is hosted with GitHub Pages. When a browser requests a page, the
          hosting provider may process connection and request data needed to deliver and protect the
          service. Depending on the request, this can include an IP address, request date and time,
          requested resource, browser or device information and referrer information sent by the browser.
        </p>
        <p>
          The purpose is reliable delivery, security, abuse prevention and technical operation. The
          intended legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR: the legitimate interest in providing a secure,
          functional website. GitHub determines its own technical logging and retention practices;
          this notice does not claim an exact retention period. See the
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>International transfers</h3>
        <p>
          GitHub is part of a group with operations in the United States. Hosting-provider processing
          may therefore involve access or transfers outside the European Economic Area. GitHub describes
          the transfer safeguards and frameworks it relies on in its privacy statement.
        </p>

        <h3>Email and phone enquiries</h3>
        <p>
          If you email or call, Be Deutsch processes the contact details, message content and any
          information you voluntarily provide in order to respond, manage the enquiry and resolve a
          support issue. Email is provided through STRATO. The legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR where
          the enquiry concerns a contract or steps before a contract, and otherwise Article 6(1)(f)
          GDPR, based on the legitimate interest in answering genuine enquiries and providing support.
        </p>
        <p>
          Correspondence is kept only as long as reasonably necessary for the enquiry and any applicable
          legal, security or record-keeping requirement. No exact STRATO retention period is asserted here.
          See the <a href="https://www.strato.de/datenschutz/" lang="de">STRATO privacy information</a>.
          Please do not send passwords or unnecessary sensitive personal information.
        </p>

        <h3>Recipients and processors</h3>
        <p>
          Website request data may be processed by GitHub as the hosting provider. Email data may
          be processed by STRATO as the email service provider. Data may also be disclosed where required
          by law or a binding request from a competent authority. Be Deutsch does not sell contact or
          website data and does not provide it to advertising or analytics services.
        </p>

        <h3>External links</h3>
        <p>
          This website can link to external services. No content from those services is embedded. Once
          you follow an external link, the destination provider is responsible for its own processing.
        </p>

        <h3 id="privacy-rights">Your GDPR rights</h3>
        <p>
          Subject to the applicable conditions, you may have rights of access, rectification, erasure,
          restriction of processing, data portability and objection. Where processing is based on consent,
          consent can be withdrawn for the future. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data
          protection supervisory authority, including in the EU member state of your habitual residence,
          place of work or the place of the alleged infringement.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section id="app-privacy" tone="canvas" labelledby="app-privacy-title">
      <div class="legal-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">B. Android app privacy</p>
        <h2 id="app-privacy-title">Be Deutsch A1 Foundations for Android</h2>
        <p class="legal-meta">Package: <code>com.bedeutsch.app</code> · App-policy effective date: 3 October 2026</p>

        <h3>Summary</h3>
        <p>
          The app is designed to work offline and stores learning progress on the Android device. It
          does not require a Be Deutsch account, does not provide cloud sync and does not send learner
          progress to Be Deutsch servers.
        </p>

        <h3>Data stored locally on the device</h3>
        <p>The app may store:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>onboarding and app settings;</li>
          <li>lesson completion and resume position;</li>
          <li>practice, quiz, checkpoint and review attempts;</li>
          <li>answers, scores, feedback and mistake categories;</li>
          <li>mistake-based review items and due dates; and</li>
          <li>progress history used to display learning status and review activity.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This information is kept in the app's private local database and is used to provide progress,
          scoring, feedback, My Mistakes and review features on that device.
        </p>

        <h3>What the app does not provide or use</h3>
        <p>
          The current app has no accounts or sign-in, cloud sync, advertising identifiers, ads,
          subscriptions, in-app purchases, social or community features, messaging, user-generated
          content, AI tutor or AI conversation. It does not request microphone, camera, contacts,
          location or general file-library access. It includes bundled offline listening audio and
          self-guided, unscored speaking and pronunciation activities. The app does not record learner
          audio, perform speech recognition or ASR, or use AI speaking analysis, so no learner voice
          data is collected or transmitted. It contains no developer-operated analytics or
          crash-reporting SDK.
        </p>

        <h3>No transmission of learning records</h3>
        <p>
          The app does not transmit learning progress, answers, scores, review history or mistake data
          to Be Deutsch, an analytics provider, an advertising provider or a Be Deutsch cloud service.
        </p>

        <h3>Android backup and restore</h3>
        <p>
          Android backup is currently permitted. Depending on device settings and the Android or Google
          backup service, app-private data may be backed up or restored by the operating-system provider.
          That processing is controlled by the relevant platform or backup provider and its terms. Be
          Deutsch cannot access data in a user's platform backup.
        </p>

        <h3>Platform diagnostics</h3>
        <p>
          Android or Google Play may process platform diagnostics such as crash or application-not-responding
          reports under the user's device and Play settings and Google's policies. The app does not include
          a developer-operated crash-reporting SDK and does not directly transmit diagnostics to Be Deutsch.
        </p>

        <h3>Sharing or sale</h3>
        <p>
          Be Deutsch does not sell app data and does not share learning records with third parties.
          Platform backup or diagnostics may be handled by the device or platform provider as described above.
        </p>

        <h3>Retention and deletion</h3>
        <p>
          Local learning data remains on the device until app storage is cleared or the app is uninstalled.
          It can be deleted through Android Settings by opening the Be Deutsch app entry and clearing its
          storage, or by uninstalling the app. Clearing storage is irreversible on that installation.
          A platform backup provider may retain or later restore a backup according to its settings and
          policies. Because Be Deutsch keeps no server-side learner record, there is no Be Deutsch cloud
          record to request for deletion.
        </p>

        <h3>Support correspondence</h3>
        <p>
          If a user emails support, the sender address, message and any voluntarily included information
          are used to respond and resolve the request. Support correspondence is separate from the offline
          learning database and is retained only as reasonably necessary for the request and applicable
          legal or security needs. Users should not send passwords or unnecessary sensitive information.
        </p>

        <h3>Children</h3>
        <p>
          The app is a general language-learning product planned for users aged 13 and older. It is not
          directed to children under 13, and Be Deutsch does not knowingly collect personal data from
          children through an app account or developer server because neither exists. The final Google Play
          target-audience settings must remain consistent with this policy before public release.
        </p>

        <h3>Security and changes</h3>
        <p>
          Local data is held in Android app-private storage and benefits from the device's Android sandbox
          and security settings, but no storage method is risk-free. Users should keep Android updated and
          use a secure screen lock. This policy will be updated if features such as accounts, cloud sync,
          analytics, ads, payments or other network services are introduced.
        </p>

        <h3 id="privacy-contact">Privacy contact</h3>
        <p>
          Questions about either section can be sent to
          <a href={`mailto:${legal.supportEmail}?subject=Be%20Deutsch%20privacy%20question`}>{legal.supportEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
